From 17afeff3238c76592239b962f5ece4a22a100439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:28:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [meta] allow \result in \postcond properties

A meta-property with \context(\postcond) is translated into an ensures
clause of each target function, but process_meta_termassoc in
meta_parse.ml built the logic typing environment from append_here_label,
append_pre_label and append_old_and_post_labels only, without calling
Logic_typing.add_result. Any \postcond predicate mentioning \result was
therefore rejected with "\result meaningless" (or collapsed to \true
under \tguard).

Thread an optional ?(with_result=false) flag from process_property
(enabled only when mp_context = Postcond) through delay_prop to
process_meta_termassoc. When set, and when the kernel function has a
function type (guarding against Cil_datatype.Kf.dummy used by
Meta_deduce.dummy_unpack, whose type is Typ.dummy rather than a TFun),
extend the environment with Logic_typing.add_result on the function's
return type (adding ghost when Kernel_function.is_ghost kf, matching
Logic_typing.funspec and Filecheck.check_ast).

- Non-void return types (scalars, top-level const, typedefs, pointers to
  const, structs and ghost functions) pass AST integrity checking
  (-check) and preserve pointed-to qualifiers and typedef names.
- Void-returning targets remain refused with "\result meaningless"
  because Logic_typing.add_result is a no-op on void (and collapse to
  \true / \false under \tguard / \fguard).
- All other contexts (\precond, \weak_invariant, \strong_invariant,
  \conditional_invariant, \writing, \reading, \calling) remain refused.

Add regression test tests/meta/postcond_result.c with its default and
fold oracles, and document the behaviour in README.md and CHANGELOG.md.
